Most of the time, I use the Linux console.  You may want to check it out, 
I personally really prefer it over any X terminal.  Of course, using 
svgatextmode to set something other than 80x25 (80x25 is best for NetHack, 
but bad for coding) and the resolution (important if on a LCD display) 
will help a lot.

And when I'm on a Windows machine, I've found Courier New to be the only 
usable font.  For me, it would be 'apt-get msttcorefonts', for you...
Google says it's 'emerge corefonts' but I may read it wrong.

And of course... you can always design your own font.  I've made a 4x5 one 
recently if you're interested (looks just great on 1600x1200!)...

